KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp26 --unwind 5
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ contracts hold: SUCCESS$
^\[sign\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition r == 1 \|\| r == -1: SUCCESS$
^\[bump\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition count >= by: SUCCESS$
^\[.*add\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition .*total >= v: SUCCESS$
^\[sum\.contract_assert\.1\] line \d+ contract assertion .*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.\d+\] line \d+ precondition x != 0: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
CBMC uses the enforce evaluation semantic ([basic.contract.eval]/2 makes
the choice implementation-defined) in C++26 mode: the contract assertions
become properties, and a violation ends the path (the program is
contract-terminated, /13).  Checked with GCC 16 -fcontracts.
